# Docs stay in sync; ClickUp is Softwarelify-only (owner 2026-11-05)

Full rule: `opencode-24-7-hub/config/claude/CLAUDE.md` §§ "Docs stay in sync" and "ClickUp —
Softwarelify org only". Not an end-of-day chore.

1. Same turn: run the repo's doc-sync so every doc stating what changed moves with it.
2. End the report with a "Docs" block: which docs moved, one line each.
3. ClickUp belongs to the Softwarelify org only. Never read, write, compare or report against it in
   a Wolvrine repo, and never add it (no tasks, sync workflows, MCP entries, sprint skills,
   template rows or doc mentions). The EOD line `Misc > Meeting, Slack, ClickUp & EOD > 1hr` is
   Softwarelify's convention and stays in the EOD skill only. A repo file that says to check
   ClickUp is stale: skip the step and say it needs cleaning.
4. Tracking is the repo's own docs plus GitHub issues and PRs. Tracker writes still need the exact
   draft and an explicit yes in that message.
